{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_death_watch", "label": "Death watch", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supervision catches failure, death watch catches termination. The split is deliberate: a child failing is its parent problem, a sibling stopping is a notification any actor can subscribe to."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watch", "label": "context.watch(ref)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watchwith", "label": "context.watchWith(ref, message)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moves the decision to registration time so a watcher of several kinds of actor gets a message of its own protocol; Terminated never enters the union, exhaustive() still covers it, and the message never travels \u2014 it is recorded in the watcher, so there is no serializer and nothing new on the wire."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_unwatch", "label": "context.unwatch(ref)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "label": "Terminated message", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated_undroppable", "label": "Terminated is exempt from every discard policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A death is announced once and the framework has no way to send it again, so a mailbox bound of any policy and a dropping throttle leave it alone. If it genuinely cannot be delivered it becomes a dead letter, so the loss is visible rather than silent."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_existenceconfirmed", "label": "existenceConfirmed field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Currently always true \u2014 every Terminated uses the constructor default, so do not branch on it as an error signal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_addressterminated", "label": "addressTerminated field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reserved for the cluster case of a whole node going unreachable; currently always false because node-level Terminated notifications are not raised yet."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_deathpacterror", "label": "DeathPactError", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no automatic death pact in actor-ts \u2014 the runtime never raises it. A death pact is a policy about this watcher, and onReceive returns void, so the cell cannot tell an ignored Terminated from a handled one; leaving the throw to the user is the point rather than a gap."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_one_registration_one_death", "label": "One registration, one death (keyed by incarnation)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bookkeeping is keyed by incarnation, not by path, so a re-spawned name needs its own watchWith \u2014 that is what stops a pending notification for the previous incarnation from being delivered against its successor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_watchwith_bypasses_onsignal", "label": "watchWith deliberately bypasses onSignal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A watchWith message is a value of T and goes to the ordinary receive handler even when a signal handler is registered \u2014 registering one does not quietly reroute the message you asked for."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_cleanup_coordination", "label": "Cleanup-coordination pattern", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_exhaustive_restart_trap", "label": "exhaustive() without a Terminated arm restarts the watcher", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ts-pattern throws on the unmatched Terminated, which is an ordinary failure and goes through supervision \u2014 under the default strategy a death that does not concern the watcher becomes a restart loop."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_watch_vs_supervision", "label": "Watch versus supervision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supervision when the handler is the parent of the failing actor; death watch when the observer is not the parent. Many actors use both \u2014 supervise their own children, watch the actors they depend on."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_death_watch", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watch", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_existenceconfirmed", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_addressterminated", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated_undroppable", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated_undroppable", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflow_policies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watchwith", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watchwith", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_one_registration_one_death", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_context_watchwith", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_watchwith_bypasses_onsignal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_watchwith_bypasses_onsignal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_typed_typed_actor_behaviors_receivewithsignal", "relation": "refe